content:
Audit state never cleared when workflowId changes or before refetching — produces cross-workflow data leakage and confusing combined render states.

Two distinct issues in this block:

1. Cross-workflow leakage. TracePanel can be reused with a different workflowId prop (the parent swaps taskId/workflowId). When that happens, auditRows / auditErr from the previous workflow remain in state and flash on screen until loadAudit completes. Clear them in a useEffect that watches workflowId, or reset at the start of loadAudit (see fix).

2. Stale-during-refetch + dual-render. loadAudit() sets auditErr=null but does NOT reset auditRows to null before fetching, so the previous list keeps rendering throughout the new request. Worse, if a previous load succeeded (auditRows !== null) and a later load fails, the render path shows BOTH the error block (lines 422-427) AND the list block (lines 436-461) simultaneously, because the conditionals are independent.

Fix sketch:
```ts
const loadAudit = () => {
  if (!workflowId) return;
  setAuditErr(null);
  setAuditRows(null); // prevent stale flash + enforce loading state
  listWorkflowAudit(workflowId, 300)
    .then(setAuditRows)
    .catch((e) => setAuditErr(String(e)));
};
```

And in the render guard, treat rows+err as mutually exclusive — e.g. hide the list when auditErr is set, so the user sees a clear error state rather than contradictory content.

The tab-click comment says "防跨工作流残留旧数据" but the implementation does the opposite — it leaves stale data in place.

